selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#profiler-adaptation-interface\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Profiler adaptation interface<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#profiler-adaptation-interface\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Adaptation has three steps, with the full call order:\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">makePlan</span> <span class=\"pre\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">doSetMode</span> <span class=\"pre\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">doStart</span> <span class=\"pre\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">startOp/stopOp</span> <span class=\"pre\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">doStop</span> <span class=\"pre\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"pre\">import</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"#declare-capabilities-and-build-a-collection-plan\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">1. Declare capabilities and build a collection plan<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#declare-capabilities-and-build-a-collection-plan\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VendorAdapter</span></code> declares supported metrics and converts a user request into an actual plan:</p>", "a[href=\"#parse-vendor-performance-data\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">3. Parse vendor performance data<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#parse-vendor-performance-data\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VendorMetricsImporter.import(metadata,</span> <span class=\"pre\">plan)</span></code> converts the vendor\u2019s raw output into a unified <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VendorProfileArtifact</span></code>. Structs such as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">SessionProfileMetadata</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VendorProfilePlan</span></code>, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">VendorProfileArtifact</span></code> are defined by FlagPrism.</p>", "a[href=\"#chip-vendor-adaptation\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Chip Vendor Adaptation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#chip-vendor-adaptation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h1><p>This page summarizes the requirements for adapting FlagPrism Profiler and Debugger to a new chip vendor, based on <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">docs/CHIP_VENDOR_ADAPTATION_REQUIREMENTS.md</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"#debugger-adaptation\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Debugger adaptation<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#debugger-adaptation\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>The Debugger path requires the vendor backend to support hidden kernel arguments (for debug pointers) and device-side debug-record writes. The runtime must allocate debug memory, pass the pointers into the kernel, and retrieve records after execution. See the backend support matrix in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Debugger/README.md</span></code> for current validation status (Ascend/CANN9 and Tianshu/CoreX 4.4 validated).</p>", "a[href=\"#goal\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Goal<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#goal\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>After adaptation, a vendor platform must support:</p>", "a[href=\"#start-collection-and-mark-operators\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">2. Start collection and mark operators<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#start-collection-and-mark-operators\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h3><p>The <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Profiler</span></code> interface implements <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">doStart()</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">doFlush()</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">doStop()</span></code>, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">doSetMode(options)</span></code>. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OpInterface</span></code> implements <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">startOp(scope)</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">stopOp(scope)</span></code> to correlate Triton ops with chip-side performance events.</p>", "a[href=\"#information-categories\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Information categories<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#information-categories\" title=\"Link to this heading\">#</a></h2><p>Basic instrumentation and numerical summary are produced by FlagPrism itself as long as the chip supports Debugger hidden arguments and debug-record writes. Metrics not provided by the vendor are marked unsupported/unavailable without affecting the other categories.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 500, interactive: false,

            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
